# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. Reproduces current production (#4455): the online
# snapshot copies committed entries but not prepared buckets. A saga that
# prepared k1 on T before the resize began and decided before the flip has no
# bucket for k1 on R, so after the flip a commit readers already saw reverts
# (and the batch reads torn) until its terminal reaches R.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicSnapshotSkipsBuckets
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: the snapshot does not carry prepared buckets, so a commit decided before the flip reverts on the resized copy
PERTURBS: SnapCopy

--- FIND
    /\ pend' = [x \in Copies |-> [s \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
                 IF x = R /\ s \in rzShards /\ pend[R][s][k] = "none"
                 THEN pend[T][s][k] ELSE pend[x][s][k]]]]
    /\ rz' = "copied"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: prepared buckets are not copied.
    /\ UNCHANGED pend
    /\ rz' = "copied"
--- END